# Row I3.2: Milo's policy in an interview call. The Work assistant's routes and the meetings list are Work's: a candidate's
# guest cookie and a caller with no session are refused before any record is read, so a call id that names no record is
# enough here (the walk's I3.2 steps use the interview's own call record for the Work-session-against-interview checks,
# which a table cannot name: its id exists only once the call starts). Statuses are what the routes give today.
GET /api/calls/h3-no-such-call/assistant/state | guest guest:kwameLive anon
GET /api/calls/h3-no-such-call/assistant/transcript | guest guest:kwameLive anon
GET /api/calls/h3-no-such-call/assistant/minutes | guest guest:kwameLive anon
POST /api/calls/h3-no-such-call/assistant/invite | guest guest:kwameLive anon | | {}
POST /api/calls/h3-no-such-call/assistant/extend | guest guest:kwameLive anon | | {}
GET /api/meetings | guest guest:kwameLive anon
